      "problem": "The discrete random variable $X\\in Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(X=1)$ can be approximated as",
      "worked_solution": "We construct an interval around $X=1$ with a radius of $0.5:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14128539/assets/511cbc0773dab19fe30f555dd3bb1389714ea46ff3748e06026aeb36521ab9d9.png)\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=1) & ≈P(1-0.5\\le Y\\le 1+0.5) \\\\  & =P(0.5\\le Y\\le 1.5).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
